The simplest way to use Gamma, is by invoking it much like one would a
compiler on the command line^[In fact the command line interface was
designed to resemble that of the GNU Compiler Collection.].  For
example, consider the following simple program:
Document: manual/scheme
```scheme
(import (gamma polyhedra) (gamma operations))

(set-curve-tolerance! 1/1000)

(define-output cube
  (intersection (cuboid 1 1 1) (sphere 7/10)))
```
Document: manual/lua
```lua
local polyhedra = require 'gamma.polyhedra'
local operations = require 'gamma.operations'

set_curve_tolerance(0.001)

output(
   "cube",
   operations.intersection(
      polyhedra.cuboid(1, 1, 1),
      polyhedra.sphere(0.7)))
```
